# The build context for the Dockerfile. `COPY . /opt/dotfiles` sits above the
# home-manager build, so every file here is a cache key: change one and the
# whole generation rebuilds. The flake reads flake.nix, flake.lock,
# home-manager/, lib/, tasks/scripts/ and tools/; the rest stays out.
#
# If a module starts reading one of these paths, delete its line here, or the
# build fails on a file that is plainly in your checkout.

# VCS state: unread (the build uses `path:`), and rewritten by every jj
# command, which would bust the cache.
.git
.jj

# Host build outputs: symlinks into the host's /nix/store.
**/result
**/result-*
**/.direnv

# Docs, agent, editor and container config, and the tasks themselves. Root
# files only: a pattern without a slash matches from the context root, so
# `justfile` leaves tools/just/justfile in, which home-manager reads.
*.md
LICENSE
VERSION
justfile
mise.toml
.editorconfig
.gitignore
.ignore
.claude/
.agents/
.vscode/
.helix/
.devcontainer.json
.devcontainer-lock.json
.devcontainer/
.envrc
.cheat/
tasks/[0-9]*

# Docker reads these itself; in the context, an edit to them would rebuild
# the generation.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# macOS
**/.DS_Store
**/._*
